WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.067 --> 00:00:02.234
-Welcome to "The Tonight Show"!

00:00:02.234 --> 00:00:03.400
Thank you very much.
That was --

00:00:03.400 --> 00:00:06.000
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:06.000 --> 00:00:07.567
-Wow!

00:00:07.567 --> 00:00:10.200
-That applause lasted longer
than Tom Brady's retirement.

00:00:10.200 --> 00:00:13.300
-Whoa!
[ Laughter ]

00:00:13.300 --> 00:00:15.167
-That's right.
Yesterday, Tom Brady

00:00:15.167 --> 00:00:16.934
called off his retirement

00:00:16.934 --> 00:00:19.167
and announced
that he will return next season

00:00:19.167 --> 00:00:21.834
to play for
the Tampa Bay Buccaneers.

00:00:21.834 --> 00:00:24.467
That's right.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:24.467 --> 00:00:26.267
That's right.

00:00:26.267 --> 00:00:29.000
Basically, Brady saw gas prices
and said, "Back to work.

00:00:29.000 --> 00:00:31.100
Here we go."
[ Laughter ]

00:00:31.100 --> 00:00:33.400
That's right, Tom Brady is back,
and once again,

00:00:33.400 --> 00:00:35.400
he made history
as the first person

00:00:35.400 --> 00:00:37.501
to ever move to Florida
and unretire.

00:00:37.501 --> 00:00:39.434
[ Laughter ]

00:00:39.434 --> 00:00:42.467
Brady's retirement
lasted 40 days.

00:00:42.467 --> 00:00:44.934
In other words, he pretty much
gave up football for Lent.

00:00:44.934 --> 00:00:47.701
[ Laughter ]

00:00:47.701 --> 00:00:50.434
Yeah, he was only retired
for six weeks.

00:00:50.434 --> 00:00:51.934
His kids are like,
"Is it something we said?

00:00:51.934 --> 00:00:54.067
I, uh..."
[ Laughter ]

00:00:54.067 --> 00:00:56.234
I have a feeling Brady's gonna
be like one of those bands

00:00:56.234 --> 00:00:57.601
that keep going
on their farewell tour.

00:00:57.601 --> 00:01:00.200
It's like, "This is our
last tour, this year.

00:01:00.200 --> 00:01:02.167
[ Laughter ]

00:01:02.167 --> 00:01:04.100
Everyone's pumped
that Brady's back.

00:01:04.100 --> 00:01:06.100
Well, except for
maybe this guy.

00:01:06.100 --> 00:01:08.601
-Hours before
Brady announced his return,

00:01:08.601 --> 00:01:11.100
an auction took place
for the football he used

00:01:11.100 --> 00:01:13.634
to throw
his final touchdown pass.

00:01:13.634 --> 00:01:19.167
The winning bid
was more than $500,000.

00:01:19.167 --> 00:01:20.834
-The auctioneer was like,
"Sold to the guy

00:01:20.834 --> 00:01:22.434
with really bad timing.
Yeah, there you go.

00:01:22.434 --> 00:01:24.000
You got it."
[ Laughter ]

00:01:24.000 --> 00:01:27.634
Yeah, it went from Tom Brady's
last touchdown ball to a ball.

00:01:27.634 --> 00:01:31.901
[ Laughter ]

00:01:31.901 --> 00:01:33.167
In other sports news,

00:01:33.167 --> 00:01:35.901
March Madness
has officially begun.

00:01:35.901 --> 00:01:37.934
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:37.934 --> 00:01:40.501
March Madness!

00:01:40.501 --> 00:01:43.801
People -- People also call it
the Big Dance,

00:01:43.801 --> 00:01:45.300
the Road to the Final Four,

00:01:45.300 --> 00:01:47.868
and Adults Yelling at
College Kids They Don't Know.

00:01:47.868 --> 00:01:49.400
You know.
[ Laughter ]

00:01:49.400 --> 00:01:52.334
Yeah, I saw that Yale made it
to the tournament this year,

00:01:52.334 --> 00:01:53.901
but only 'cause their dad
made a phone call.

00:01:53.901 --> 00:01:57.300
[ Laughter ]

00:01:57.300 --> 00:02:00.567
Well, switching gears,
Uber just announced

00:02:00.567 --> 00:02:02.834
that customers will pay
an additional charge

00:02:02.834 --> 00:02:05.767
to help its drivers
offset high gas prices.

00:02:05.767 --> 00:02:08.434
Yeah, Uber's adding
a surcharge for gas.

00:02:08.434 --> 00:02:09.801
You know it's bad
when the driver shows up

00:02:09.801 --> 00:02:11.334
on foot and says,
"Let's take your car."

00:02:11.334 --> 00:02:13.868
[ Laughter ]

00:02:13.868 --> 00:02:15.133
"That's a nice one."

00:02:15.133 --> 00:02:16.467
Yep, things are rough now.

00:02:16.467 --> 00:02:19.200
If you want heat or A.C.,
the driver just blows on you.

00:02:19.200 --> 00:02:20.467
[ Laughter ]

00:02:20.467 --> 00:02:24.000
[ Exhaling heavily ]

00:02:24.000 --> 00:02:26.367
Some more business news --
I read that, due to inflation,

00:02:26.367 --> 00:02:30.067
Doritos has been putting
five fewer chips in each bag.

00:02:30.067 --> 00:02:32.567
[ Laughter ]

00:02:32.567 --> 00:02:34.400
And if you noticed the change,

00:02:34.400 --> 00:02:35.968
you've got bigger problems
than inflation.

00:02:35.968 --> 00:02:37.667
[ Laughter ]

00:02:37.667 --> 00:02:39.467
"W-W-What?!

00:02:39.467 --> 00:02:42.701
Normally,
there's 48 chips in the bag."

00:02:42.701 --> 00:02:45.634
-"I've been robbed!"
-"I'm only counting 43."

00:02:45.634 --> 00:02:47.501
[ Laughter ]

00:02:47.501 --> 00:02:48.634
-"Mother!"

00:02:48.634 --> 00:02:49.934
[ Laughter ]

00:02:49.934 --> 00:02:52.634
-Even worse, today, at
the grocery store, I saw this --

00:02:52.634 --> 00:02:53.634
one Pringle.

00:02:53.634 --> 00:02:56.267
[ Laughter ]

00:02:56.267 --> 00:02:57.968
One --
-Just says "Pringle."

00:02:57.968 --> 00:03:00.901
-Yeah, Pringle.
-Not Pringles.

00:03:00.901 --> 00:03:02.534
Yeah, still hard to get
your hand in there, too.

00:03:02.534 --> 00:03:04.067
I don't know why.
[ Laughter ]

00:03:04.067 --> 00:03:05.701
-And it's still broken.

00:03:05.701 --> 00:03:09.300
-Get this -- today,
Apple released an update

00:03:09.300 --> 00:03:11.834
that lets you use Face ID
to unlock your phone

00:03:11.834 --> 00:03:14.267
while wearing a mask.
-Ooh.

00:03:14.267 --> 00:03:16.000
-Even the guy who bought
Tom Brady's football

00:03:16.000 --> 00:03:17.067
was like, "Great timing."

00:03:17.067 --> 00:03:22.300
[ Laughter ]

00:03:22.300 --> 00:03:24.667
Meanwhile, I saw that the TSA
issued a statement

00:03:24.667 --> 00:03:27.400
asking spring break travelers
to be respectful.

00:03:27.400 --> 00:03:31.601
[ Laughter ]

00:03:31.601 --> 00:03:33.501
They tried putting up a sign,
but spring breakers

00:03:33.501 --> 00:03:34.667
immediately drew a penis on it.

00:03:34.667 --> 00:03:36.200
And they were like,
"All right, all right.

00:03:36.200 --> 00:03:39.868
"We get it, we get it.
We get it."

00:03:39.868 --> 00:03:41.133
I heard about a man in Florida

00:03:41.133 --> 00:03:43.801
who was arrested after
he called 9-1-1 to check

00:03:43.801 --> 00:03:45.901
if the meth
that he bought was authentic.

00:03:45.901 --> 00:03:48.601
[ Laughter ]

00:03:48.601 --> 00:03:50.601
In other words, spring break
has officially sprung.

00:03:50.601 --> 00:03:52.934
It's happening.
It's spring break.

00:03:52.934 --> 00:03:58.701
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:58.701 --> 00:04:01.901
The guy was so embarrassed,
he sent his friends this emoji.

00:04:01.901 --> 00:04:08.200
[ Laughter ]

00:04:08.200 --> 00:04:11.901
And finally, a woman in the U.K.
who just turned 102 says

00:04:11.901 --> 00:04:16.167
she credits her good health to
Jagerbombs, tequila, and pizza.

00:04:16.167 --> 00:04:23.033
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:23.033 --> 00:04:24.801
Yeah, then Prince Charles
was like, "Okay, Mum,

00:04:24.801 --> 00:04:25.968
let's get you to bed."

00:04:25.968 --> 00:04:27.133
All right,
we have a great show, everyone!

